{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLNotationsV4ItemO10arpeggiateyAeA13MXLArpeggiateVcAEmF","symbolKind":"case","roleHeading":"Case","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"arpeggiate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alternative."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLNotations","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","abstract":[{"text":"Notations refer to musical notations, not XML notations. Multiple notations are allowed in order to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiple editorial levels. The print-object attribute, added in Version 3.0, allows notations to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"details of performance technique, such as fingerings, without having them appear in the score.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item/arpeggiate(_:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"arpeggiate"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","text":"MXLArpeggiate"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"arpeggiate"},{"type":"text","text":" alternative."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate","abstract":[{"text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item","abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Notations.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}